- How would you monitor actual error in production without degrading performance?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design streaming data structures with sliding windows, handling batched updates, and rigorous amortized analysis. Also probes correctness under expirations and the practical choice between exact maintenance vs rebuilds.

## Key Concepts
- Sliding window frequency tables, heap with lazy deletion, batch amortized analysis, memory locality, worst-case scenarios.

## Code Example
```javascript
class TopFreqWindow {
  constructor(W) { this.W = W; this.cnt = new Map(); this.queue = []; this.heap = new MaxHeap(); }
  batchInsert(vals) {
    for (const v of vals) {
      this.queue.push(v);
      this.cnt.set(v, (this.cnt.get(v) || 0) + 1);
      this.heap.push({ value: v, count: this.cnt.get(v) });
    }
    this.expireIfNeeded();
  }
  expireIfNeeded() {
    while (this.queue.length > this.W) {
      const old = this.queue.shift();
      const c = (this.cnt.get(old) || 0) - 1;
      if (c <= 0) this.cnt.delete(old); else this.cnt.set(old, c);
      this.heap.push({ value: old, count: c });
    }
  }
  top1() {
    while (true) {
      const t = this.heap.peek(); if (!t) return null;
      if ((this.cnt.get(t.value) || 0) === t.count) return t.value;
      this.heap.pop();
    }
  }
}
```

